# OIBSIP Data Science Internship — Task 5

# Sales Prediction Using Python

## 📌 Project Overview

This project is completed as part of the **Oasis Infobyte Data Science Internship**.

The objective of this task is to build machine learning regression models that predict product sales based on advertising expenditure across different media channels.

The project analyzes the relationship between:

- 📺 TV advertising
- 📻 Radio advertising
- 📰 Newspaper advertising
- 💰 Product Sales

The analysis includes exploratory data analysis, data visualization, machine learning model development, model evaluation, residual analysis, and feature importance.

---

## 🎯 Objective

The main objective is to develop a regression model capable of predicting product sales based on advertising spending.

The project answers questions such as:

- Does advertising expenditure affect sales?
- Which advertising channel has the strongest relationship with sales?
- How accurately can sales be predicted?
- Which machine learning model performs better?
- Which advertising channel contributes most to the prediction?

---

## 📊 Dataset

The project uses the **Advertising dataset**, which contains information about advertising expenditure and product sales.

### Dataset Features

| Feature | Description |
|---|---|
| `TV` | Advertising expenditure on TV |
| `Radio` | Advertising expenditure on Radio |
| `Newspaper` | Advertising expenditure on Newspaper |
| `Sales` | Product sales |

The dataset contains **200 observations**.

### Dataset Source

The dataset is the classic `Advertising.csv` dataset associated with *An Introduction to Statistical Learning*.

Official source:

https://www.statlearning.com/

